From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 19:16:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: bridge the six sub-interfaces -- calls, UT, config,
 ECBM, multi-endpoint

CallSessionWrapper delegates all 28 legacy call-session methods onto ImsCallSessionImplBase, whose
no-op defaults cover everything 13 added (RTT, transfer, call quality) that 7.1 has no notion of.
CallSessionListenerAdapter carries the 30 callbacks back; all thirty exist on 13 with matching
shape. The session argument is resolved to the wrapper we already built rather than a fresh one, so
object identity stays stable and the telephony stack can match callbacks to calls; only the new
sessions handed over by merge and conference extension get their own wrapper.

UtWrapper is 16 delegations onto ImsUtImplBase. ConfigWrapper is pure delegation -- 13's IImsConfig
is method-for-method what 7.1 had, and ImsConfigListener likewise.

EcbmWrapper and MultiEndpointWrapper are shaped differently than expected: setListener on those two
ImplBase classes lives on an inner Stub, not as an overridable, because the base owns the listener
itself and exposes enteredEcbm()/onImsExternalCallStateUpdate() for the implementation to call. So
each registers its own adapter with the legacy service and forwards into the base. The legacy
external-call callback carries a raw List -- AIDL erases the element type -- so entries are checked
rather than cast wholesale.

Three things deliberately do not forward, each logged rather than silently dropped:
getVideoCallProvider returns null (7.1's provider is a different interface; video is unreachable
before VoLTE works), registrationFeatureCapabilityChanged has no 13 equivalent, and
removeRegistrationListener cannot be expressed -- 7.1 offers only setRegistrationListener, which
replaces the single listener rather than detaching one of several.

Transaction codes re-verified against the stock binary after all of it: 14 interfaces still match.
